# Line-ending normalisation — kept identical across every Cambrian repo.
#
# The sibling repos disagreed: cambrian-core was CRLF, ui/ and cli/ were LF. Since
# ui/ and cli/ VENDOR core's operator.proto, every cross-repo comparison reported
# the whole file as changed and hid the real drift inside the noise.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` normalises to LF in the repository and on checkout, and
# overrides core.autocrlf, so the tree is identical on every platform.
#
# Adopting on an existing checkout (CLEAN tree only — this rewrites most files):
#     git add --renormalize . && git commit -m "chore: normalise line endings to LF"

* text=auto eol=lf

*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.zip  binary
*.gz   binary
*.rar  binary
*.exe  binary
*.dll  binary
*.so   binary
*.dylib binary
*.db   binary
